  "model-ode": [
    {
      "preceding_text": "We used the following assumptions to examine how secretion composition and sensor preference affect paired responses. Here, (q_3) and (q_{18}) denote per-individual ligand-release rates, while (w_3) and (w_{18}) denote a sensor’s input weights for the two ligands.",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Simulation setting",
          "Value",
          "Basis"
        ],
        [
          "Combined per-individual release of the two ligands",
          "(q_3+q_{18}=1) fmol individual(^{-1}) h(^{-1}) for both Mi and Ce",
          "Common simulation scale selected for this project"
        ],
        [
          "Ligand-release ratios",
          "Mi: (q_3:q_{18}=1:10); Ce: (q_3:q_{18}=10:1)",
          "Literature provides qualitative context [3,4]; exact ratios are project assumptions"
        ],
        [
          "Sensor-response weights",
          "P3: ((w_3,w_{18})=(2/3,1/3)); P18: ((1/3,2/3))",
          "Complementary weights assigned according to the candidate preference directions"
        ]
      ],
      "source_workbook": "workspace/evidence/model-refresh-20261020/originals/Model -_ ODE and Dual-Channel Model-word/Microsoft_Excel_Worksheet1.xlsx",
      "sha256": "aec87fbaa1edf2cfa9c1772ec9c07fc11ac5d4b212a1dad2445750ffe1caeb54",
      "empty": false
    },
    {
      "preceding_text": "To assess the contribution of the second channel, we compared P3-only, P18-only, and dual-channel regression using the same training set and 19 additional simulated mixtures excluded from regression fitting. Their evaluation RMSEs were 36.591, 28.429, and 3.008 individuals per 100 cm³ of soil, respectively. The lower dual-channel error indicates that the paired responses helped distinguish target and background contributions under the assumed conditions. All evaluation mixtures were generated by the same deterministic ODE model.",
      "rows": [
        [
          "Regression model",
          "Training RMSE, 45 mixtures",
          "Evaluation RMSE, 19 mixtures"
        ],
        [
          "P3 only",
          39.511,
          36.591
        ],
        [
          "P18 only",
          29.138,
          28.429
        ],
        [
          "P3 and P18",
          3.924,
          3.008
        ]
      ],
